---
// One Postgres update is several physical writes; replicas replay the same WAL,
// so the same bytes cross the network once per replica.
// Replica count (3) is illustrative. Plain inline SVG with site tokens, no ids.
import DiagramIcon from './DiagramIcon.astro';

const W = 900;
const H = 372;
const reps = [
  { y: 80, en: 'Replica 1', vi: 'Replica 1' },
  { y: 160, en: 'Replica 2', vi: 'Replica 2' },
  { y: 240, en: 'Replica 3', vi: 'Replica 3' },
];
const rh = 60;
const rx = 640;
const midY = 160 + rh / 2;
---
<figure class="rf">
  <div class="rf-scroll">
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="One update in Postgres produces four physical writes in the primary's write-ahead log. Each replica replays that same log, so the same four writes cross the network to every replica.">
    <text x="20" y="24" class="rf-h">
      <tspan data-lang-en>Where the extra writes travel</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Những lần ghi thừa đi tới đâu</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x="20" y="46" class="rf-sub">
      <tspan data-lang-en>One update to birth_year, followed from the primary to its replicas.</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Một lệnh update birth_year, đi từ primary tới các replica.</tspan>
    </text>

    <rect x="20" y="130" width="190" height="80" rx="4" class="rf-box" />
    <DiagramIcon name="postgres" x={52} y={170} size={32} />
    <text x="82" y="165" class="rf-in">Postgres</text>
    <text x="82" y="186" class="rf-in-m">
      <tspan data-lang-en>primary</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>máy chính</tspan>
    </text>

    <path d="M210,170 L262,170" class="rf-arrow" /><polygon points="261,165 261,175 269,170" class="rf-head" />

    <rect x="270" y="120" width="230" height="100" rx="4" class="rf-box is-hot" />
    <DiagramIcon name="log" x={302} y={152} size={28} />
    <text x="330" y="148" class="rf-in">
      <tspan data-lang-en>Write-ahead log</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Write-ahead log</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x="330" y="168" class="rf-in-m is-hot">
      <tspan data-lang-en>4 physical writes</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>4 lần ghi vật lý</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x="285" y="196" class="rf-in-s">
      <tspan data-lang-en>1 row + 3 index entries</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>1 dòng + 3 entry index</tspan>
    </text>

    {reps.map((r) => (
      <g>
        <path d={`M500,170 L560,170 L560,${r.y + rh / 2} L631,${r.y + rh / 2}`} class="rf-arrow is-hot" />
        <polygon points={`630,${r.y + rh / 2 - 5} 630,${r.y + rh / 2 + 5} 638,${r.y + rh / 2}`} class="rf-head is-hot" />
        <rect x={rx} y={r.y} width="240" height={rh} rx="4" class="rf-box" />
        <DiagramIcon name="server" x={rx + 30} y={r.y + rh / 2} size={28} />
        <text x={rx + 58} y={r.y + 26} class="rf-in">
          <tspan data-lang-en>{r.en}</tspan>
          <tspan data-lang-vi>{r.vi}</tspan>
        </text>
        <text x={rx + 58} y={r.y + 46} class="rf-in-m">
          <tspan data-lang-en>replays all 4 writes</tspan>
          <tspan data-lang-vi>chạy lại cả 4 lần ghi</tspan>
        </text>
      </g>
    ))}
    <text x="570" y="68" class="rf-note is-hot" text-anchor="middle">
      <tspan data-lang-en>over the network</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>qua mạng</tspan>
    </text>

    <line x1="20" x2={W - 20} y1="318" y2="318" class="rf-rule" />
    <text x="20" y="344" class="rf-note">
      <tspan data-lang-en>The number of replicas is illustrative. Klitzke calls this "a replication amplification problem".</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Số replica chỉ để minh hoạ. Klitzke gọi đây là "bài toán khuếch đại sao chép".</tspan>
    </text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Every replica replays the same log, so one small update is paid for again on each machine and on each link between them.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Mỗi replica chạy lại cùng một log, nên một update nhỏ phải trả giá thêm trên từng máy và từng đường truyền giữa chúng.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .rf { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .rf-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .rf svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; }
  .rf text { font-size: 14px; fill: var(--text-body); }
  .rf .rf-h { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .rf .rf-sub { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .rf-rule { stroke: var(--border); }
  .rf-box { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .rf-box.is-hot { fill: var(--red-tint-bg); stroke: var(--red); stroke-width: 1.6; }
  .rf .rf-in { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; fill: var(--text); }
  .rf .rf-in-m { font-size: 13px; fill: var(--text-body); }
  .rf .rf-in-m.is-hot { fill: var(--red); font-weight: 700; }
  .rf .rf-in-s { font-size: 12.5px; fill: var(--text-body); }
  .rf .rf-note { font-size: 13px; fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .rf .rf-note.is-hot { fill: var(--red); font-weight: 600; }
  .rf-arrow { fill: none; stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .rf-arrow.is-hot { stroke: var(--red); stroke-width: 1.6; }
  .rf-head { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .rf-head.is-hot { fill: var(--red); }
  .rf figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
